it's michelle of lab muffin beauty  science here chemistry phd cosmetic  chemist and big fan of asian skin care  today i'm going to be talking about my  favorite hamish products hamish is a  korean brand that's best known for their  cleansing balm it has a cult following  and obviously i'll be talking about that  but they have a lot of other really  interesting products too this video is  sponsored by star korean an online  korean beauty store that stops hamish  along with tons of other brands like and  subscribe and click the notification  bell so you know when new videos go up  i'm going to start with the hamish all  clean balm this is hamish's most popular  product and lots of people have this as  their all-time favorite cleansing balm  and for good reason i've been using this  for years i don't think i've ever  reviewed it though and i should really  do a video on my favorite cleansing  balms but this one is very high up there  in case you didn't already know  cleansing balms are great for quickly  getting makeup and waterproof sunscreen  off your face really fast i talked about  this before in my cleansing mist video  but you don't actually need to use an  oil-based cleanser to remove makeup and  sunscreen a lot of the time regular  cleansers will work fine and you can  even remove them with microfiber cloths  and plain water but a lot of people  including me really like using oil based  cleansers for that because it feels  really effortless and the oil massage is  really relaxing so how you use these you  scoop out a small amount of the  cleansing balm then you massage it over  your dry dirty face at the start of your  cleansing routine the solid balm will  melt on your skin as you rub and it  turns into an oil then you rinse it off  with warm water i personally rub the  balm on before i get into the shower and  then i rinse it off in the shower and  you'll see the water go milky as it  emulsifies and the all droplets go into  the water you can follow up with a  regular cleanser like a foaming cleanser  which i do if i'm wearing makeup or if  you think your skin is clean enough you  can just leave it which is what i do if  i didn't leave the house and i didn't  wear sunscreen or makeup that day this  balm is a really good cleansing balm  that works really well to get rid of  waterproof makeup including mascara and  it rinses off really cleanly some  cleansing bars will leave a bit of oil  on your face and depending on the  product you can either leave this on  your face or you might prefer to get it  off with a follow-up cleanser i've  personally found that it really depends  on which balm i'm using whether or not i  break out with that extra oil but with  this one you don't have a layer left  behind so you don't need to worry about  it this is just one of the more  affordable cleansing balms that works  really well it's slightly centered it  has this flip top lid that makes it  really easy to get into it has a little  spot for storing your spatula if you're  a neat person who's not into digging out  the product with your fingers or just  like  smashing the spatula in there for  storage this product does have  polyethylene in it i'll talk more about  it in a future video because it's a bit  of a complicated topic but  very briefly this has a form of  polyethylene in it but there are lots of  different types of polyethylene and the  type in cleansing balms is probably  somewhat biodegradable it's a less solid  form than microbeads so the  environmental impacts are quite  different the amount in it is also  really small compared to the other  microplastics you generally produce in  the rest of your life so while i'd like  it if brands replaced it with more  degradable ingredients it isn't really a  big deal breaker for me i tried a bunch  of hamish's cleansers and these two are  my favorites this is the ph 5.5 all  clean green foam i really like that this  has a low skin friendly ph of 5.5  because a lot of asian cleansers tend to  have really high ph's high ph will  disrupt your skin a bit more than a  lower ph that matches your skin's ph  this foams nicely it cleanses nicely and  it doesn't leave my skin feeling tight  afterwards it is fragrance free and it  smells a bit plasticky as i've mentioned  before i do prefer a mild fragrance in  my cleanses to not have that smell this  is just very functional i think it's a  great option i personally find it a bit  boring but for a lot of people no frills  is exactly what you want in a cleanser  and if that's you i highly recommend  this there's also the all clean white  clay foam i actually like this a bit  more than the other one this is a  foaming cleanser that has two types of  clay in it which is bentonite and kaolin  so it soaks up oil as you clean it's  sort of like a way of getting the  benefits of a clay mask while you're  cleansing so  i love lazy products this does have a  high ph it's around eight or nine but  this is probably the nicest feeling high  ph cleanser i've ever tried it's soap  based but the soap's been mixed with  other non-soap surfactants which should  reduce the soap disrupting your skin  this also has glycerin in it which stops  your skin from getting too dehydrated  while cleansing i've talked about how  formulations can make surfactants work  gently in my cleanse and mist video as  well i didn't find this drying or tight  but i did try it during an australian  summer which is pretty humid and i have  oily skin i did try a couple of other  high ph soap based cleansers over the  last few months and they haven't worked  as well as this so i do think this is  actually gentler and i was actually  quite surprised it didn't feel tight  even though there is that clay in it  this also has hydrolyzed silk and  hyaluronic acid which would help keep  your skin hydrated as well  it has a light scent which comes from  essential oils and so i'd recommend this  for people with oily skin maybe go for  the other one if you have dry skin or  you're sensitive to fragrance moving on  to moisturizers hamish have a whole  bunch of really nice moisturizers and  these are my favorites one thing i love  about asian skincare is that there are a  lot of gel moisturizers available that  are really good for early dehydration  prone skin and just hot weather in  general standard moisturizers are  usually creams or lotions that are oil  in water emulsions and these use  traditional emulsifiers to keep all  droplets suspended in the product these  traditional emulsifiers can sometimes  feel pretty heavy with a gel cream the  oil droplets get suspended using a  network of special polymers and this  ends up feeling a lot lighter on your  skin gel creams are a lot more popular  in asia there aren't a ton of gel cream  options available at a lower price point  in australia so i was really excited to  try the watermelon moisture soothing gel  cream this is fantastic it used to be  called the moisture surge gel cream and  it's very similar to the clinique  version this has a very lightweight  texture but it's really hydrating  there's lots of glycerin in it and it  leaves behind a satiny hydrated looking  finish on my skin it doesn't peel i'm  actually wearing it now under my makeup  it's fragrance free and the smell is not  very offensive for a fragrance-free  product i also really like the all clean  vitamin blemish spot clear cream this is  a slightly heavier cream it's more  moisturizing but again it's really  hydrating with lots of glycerin it feels  really cooling when you put it on your  skin and i think i could still probably  use it as a heavier day cream this has a  light scent and it has five percent  niacinamide and vitamin c which comes  from kakadu plum extract it's actually  approved as a functional cosmetic in  korea for brightening and anti-wrinkle  claims and i believe that's because it  contains two to five percent niacinamide  and 0.04 adenosine but it does also have  clinical testing on the box which you  can see on this graph  and that shows that it has a modest  decrease in pigment and you can also see  some before and afters on the hamish  website the box also shows the  irritation testing and i think this is  just a really nice moisturizer i love  that you can get a high percentage of  niacinamide in one product which means  you can sort of spend your serums on  other ingredients moving on to the  marine care cream toner  this is a newer sort of product for me  it's a toner that has a lot of oil in it  but it's very watery as you can see but  it moisturizes a lot more like a lotion  this product is very similar to the  laneige cream skin which i also love  they both have very similar top line  moisturizing ingredients which are  butylene glycol and glycerin as  humectants as well as meta foam seed oil  as the oil component it's also approved  as a functional cosmetic for brightening  and anti-wrinkle in korea which i'm  guessing means that the niacinamide in  this is between two and five percent and  the adenosine is at 0.04  it also has marine extracts in it and  according to the packaging it's in  liposomal form which means they're  bundled up in little packets which  supposedly should deliver better into  your skin this also has a very mild  scent whereas the laneige is fragrance  free but on my skin the moisturizing  effect is pretty much the same for both  so i guess your choice would depend on  whether you want more actors and how you  feel about fragrance i also tried the  marine care eye cream i usually don't  use eye creams because i wear contact  lenses at night and if any product gets  into my eyes it is a massive pain i have  to go through the whole contact lens  removal and reinsertion process but i  gave this one a go because it has a  thicker texture and so i figured it  probably wouldn't travel as much and i  was right this does hydrate my under eye  area pretty nicely without traveling  into my eyes this also has that  niacinamide and adenosine combo that  makes it a functional cosmetic it also  has marine extracts and peptides again  it has that liposomal technology which  should deliver that deeper into your  skin this does have a moderate scent but  because you don't use very much product  it's not super noticeable it comes with  a metal de-puffing massage stick and  this is quite soothing i found myself  using it during the day when i was in  front of the computer and my eyes were  getting a bit tired i prefer applying  this cream by pressing it in with my  fingers because the texture is a bit  thick and so it's a bit difficult to  spread with the stick but massaging it  in with the cool stick afterwards is  really nice i don't think you  necessarily need a separate eye cream  unless you have the same problem as me  where your face likes products that  slide around but your eyes don't and i  guess i'm just not really an eye cream  connoisseur because i haven't tried that  many but i did find myself really  enjoying this i found myself reaching  for it a lot more than i expected my  final pick from the hamish range of the  products i tried is the black tea mask  pack  this has a really puree fluffy sorbet  sort of texture  it is moderately strongly scented and  it's quite a floral scent to use it you  apply it for five to ten minutes and  then you wash it off i wiped it off with  a damp cloth or cotton pad and i've  heard that some people leave this on  overnight i wasn't expecting a lot from  this product because you are only meant  to use it for five to ten minutes but i  was really impressed by how hydrating it  was in such a short amount of time the  effect this had was kind of like a sheet  mask without being a sheet mask i think  i've mentioned before how i don't really  like sheet masks because they're kind of  fussy to me i know a lot of people like  to relax with a sheet mask on but i find  that i don't really relax which  i know sounds kind of bad but i like to  do things while i relax like i like to  read or crochet and i don't like the  distraction of the feeling of the sheet  mask sliding down a layer of this feels  just like moisturizer and i found that  this gave me a lot of those hydrating  skin smoothing effects that shade masks  tend to give i haven't used a lot of  masks recently because they are just to  me a lot of effort but this is like a  really low effort mask that still  delivers a lot of benefits so those are  my favorite hamish products so far all  the links to buy are in the description  and they're currently on sale at style  korean let me know if you've tried any  of these products before and what you  thought of them i've also got some more  reviews of asian skincare products in  the description you can follow me on  instagram tiktok check out my blog and  see you next time for more nerdy beauty  talk

